<%/* Upgrade the app's Koda, asked first in the modal (D-k7v): it starts a
     fix, "Upgrade Koda to <latest>", on a branch of its own. Prelude installs
     the new version in the fix's worktree with the project's package manager
     (`koda.install`, a fixed command that names only Koda), then the agent
     changes the app's views where the new version needs it. The person's own
     folder isn't touched until the fix is merged (R-q7w). Clicking Upgrade
     approves the command it shows. Reached when there's nothing to upgrade,
     or with an upgrade already under way, it says so. Started, the modal
     closes and the app card links to the fix. The app names the fix and its
     branch itself. `it` is the project. */%>
<% const p = it, koda = p.app?.koda; %>
<div class="stack gap-4">
<% if (koda?.upgradeUrl) { %>
  <h2>Koda is already being upgraded</h2>
  <p class="secondary">A fix is upgrading this app to Koda <%= koda.latest %> on <code><%= koda.upgradeBranch %></code>. Carry on with it there, or discard it under In progress to start again.</p>
  <div class="cluster actions">
    <a class="btn" href="<%= koda.upgradeUrl %>">Open the fix</a>
    <button class="btn ghost" type="button" command="--koda-empty" commandfor="modal">Back to the project</button>
  </div>
<% } else if (koda?.behind) { %>
  <h2>Upgrade Koda to <%= koda.latest %>?</h2>
  <p class="secondary">This app uses Koda <%= koda.version %>. Upgrading starts a fix on a branch of its own, where the agent reads <%= koda.latest %>’s guidance and changes the app’s views where it needs to. You check them and finish the fix like any other.</p>
  <div class="notice warn">
    <p>Prelude runs <code><%= koda.install %></code> in the fix’s copy of <code><%= p.app.path ? `${p.app.path}/` : 'the project' %></code>. Installing runs code from the package registry. Your own folder isn’t changed: once the fix is merged, the app card offers to install <%= koda.latest %> there too.</p>
  </div>
  <form class="cluster actions" action="/f/<%= p.id %>/app/koda" method="post">
    <button class="btn primary" type="submit">Upgrade Koda</button>
    <button class="btn ghost" type="button" command="--koda-empty" commandfor="modal">Not now</button>
  </form>
<% } else { %>
  <h2>Nothing to upgrade</h2>
  <p class="secondary"><%= koda?.version ? `This app already uses Koda ${koda.version}, the version Prelude knows.` : 'This app doesn’t use Koda.' %></p>
  <div class="cluster actions">
    <button class="btn" type="button" command="--koda-empty" commandfor="modal">Back to the project</button>
  </div>
<% } %>
</div>
